    'Ran a second actual composed refinement. It supplied usable S/E material but N again introduced an uncanonical mid-body fin-like marking/proportions. That geometry is rejected; repeated drift returns to exact constructed anatomy rather than another prompt loop or masking away an AI limb. No N generated pixels, contours, new marks, alpha or proportions enter production. No fake third generation/second isolation. '
    'Initial selected S material specimen caught a white fleck; retained initial selection and registration as rejected experiment. Corrected opaque unmarked S cheek sample inspected, with only bounded gray residual transferred through eroded canonical skin. Canonical fin-ray shading, exact six flecks, head/barbels, silhouettes and alpha remain fixed. Manual near-gray ink and all production surfaces normalize to equal RGB. '
    'Registered all four directions on one768square frame with trunk/swim pivot384,384 and authored1.2square worldcanvas. E/N are exact whole-animal turns of the selected normal body; W mirrors E. No per-facing bounds fit, size change, human foot pivot, independent head turn or new articulated fin/limb/head nodes. Two neutral colour planes draw one whole animal with the same animation transform. '
    'Explicit alpha-over decomposition retains source primary m and detail C roles without doubled coverage or carved limb holes. Neutral layer assembly exactly equals gray master in all views and has zero alpha error; native m/C preview differs by at most1gray level on covered RGB due8bit tint rounding. No fixed-colour pixels/fallback, water tint or baked glow remain. Palette OFF/ON and intended-size/source comparisons reviewed. '
